Use objcopy's --output-target when converting the ELF shared object to an
EFI application. --target sets both the input and output format, so the
ELF input is claimed to be efi-app-*. binutils 2.46 and newer check the
input target strictly and reject it:

  objcopy: HelloWorld.so: file format not recognized

Gentoo and Debian carry the same one-line fix:
https://bugs.gentoo.org/970040
https://bugs.debian.org/1122408

Context is kept to one line because src_prepare rewrites the adjacent
LDFLAGS line before PATCHES are applied.

BUG=b:553084273

--- a/Make.rules
+++ b/Make.rules
@@ -28,3 +28,3 @@
 LOADLIBES	= -lefi -lgnuefi $(shell $(CC) $(ARCH3264) -print-libgcc-file-name)
-FORMAT		= --target=efi-app-$(ARCH)
+FORMAT		= --output-target=efi-app-$(ARCH)
 OBJCOPY		= objcopy
